  "summary": "The paper introduces the fully-inductive setup for node classification in graph machine learning, where models must generalize to arbitrary test graphs with different structures, feature, and label spaces. The proposed model, GraphAny, uses a combination of LinearGNNs and an inductive attention module with entropy-normalized distance features. It achieves strong performance on diverse datasets, outperforming both inductive and transductive baselines.",
  "strengths": [
    "Introduces a novel and challenging setup (fully-inductive) that generalizes to arbitrary graphs with different structures, features, and labels.",
    "Proposes a novel model architecture (GraphAny) that combines analytical solutions with learned inductive attention.",
    "Demonstrates strong empirical results, including surpassing transductive models trained on each dataset individually.",
    "Provides detailed ablation studies and comparisons with baselines, validating the importance of key components like entropy normalization and attention parameterization."
